What are the possible risks or discomforts I may experience during the study?
There may be risks or discomforts that are currently unforeseeable at this time. We will tell you about any significant new information we learn that may relate to your willingness to continue participating in this study.

What are the benefits of participation in the study?
It is hoped that the information gained in this study will benefit society by advancing the knowledge in how AI systems can enhance the educational experience of students and teachers. While also providing additional back-bone support to debate on whether or not AI should be integrated/implemented/put into students' education.
You may benefit from this research by gaining a better understanding of important Computer Science Concepts. Better understanding of Cybersecurity, Front-End development, Back-End development, and Full Stack development. However, these benefits are not fixed, meaning participants may not benefit from this, these are just possibilities.
What measures will be taken to ensure the confidentiality of the data or to protect my privacy?
Research records identifying participants will be kept confidential to the extent permitted by applicable laws and regulations and will not be made publicly available without your permission. However, it is possible that other people and offices responsible for making sure research is done safely and responsibly will see your information, which is the AP Research organization.
To protect confidentiality of the study records and data, the following measures will be taken: Every record will be saved on paper that will be put into a folder and put away in a secure location such as a locked cabinet, also data will be transferred to a digital spreadsheet that will put in a google drive folder that will only be accessed by the owner and not shared with any other personnel/people, also when you are mention in a paper, it will be of a coded name, such as if a student was named, “Donzell” it may be changed to, “participant01”. These records will be kept indefinitely, meaning it will not be destroyed, it will be kept for evidence, there is no risk to the subjects.


To protect your confidentiality when results of the study are reported, the following measures will be taken: confidentiality will be maintained even after research is over and will follow the same measures as said before.

Will the information I provide be used for anything other than the current study?
Information about you, including your biospecimens, will only be used by the research team for the project described in this document. 
